Found while investigating karr #7. lib/WWW/MetaForge/ArcRaiders/Result/Quest.pm from_hashref (line ~101) reads $data->{grantedItems}, $data->{createdAt}, $data->{updatedAt}, $data->{markerCategory}, $data->{guideLinks}, $data->{traderName}, $data->{sortOrder}, $data->{requiredItems} -- camelCase keys.

Verified via curl against the live, free API (https://metaforge.app/api/arc-raiders/quests?limit=100, all 100 quests checked) that the actual response uses snake_case throughout: granted_items, created_at, updated_at, marker_category, guide_links, trader_name, sort_order, required_items. t/fixtures/quests.json already correctly uses snake_case too. So these 8 attributes are silently always undef/empty on every real Result::Quest object, regardless of what the API actually sends -- id/name/objectives/xp happen to be spelled the same in both conventions, which is why this was not caught.

Fix: remap from_hashref to the real snake_case keys. Add/extend a t/14-arcraiders-result-quest.t assertion against a fixture item with non-empty granted_items/guide_links/trader_name/sort_order/required_items so a regression cannot silently reintroduce this (the current test apparently does not assert on these fields, or asserts against undef and treats it as correct).

Fixed: Result::Quest::from_hashref read camelCase keys (grantedItems, createdAt, updatedAt, markerCategory, guideLinks, traderName, sortOrder, requiredItems) that the live API never sends. Changed all 8 to their snake_case equivalents (granted_items, created_at, updated_at, marker_category, guide_links, trader_name, sort_order, required_items), matching the attribute names and t/fixtures/quests.json which were already correct. Verified with perl -c and a from_hashref smoke test using snake_case keys: all 8 attributes now return real values instead of undef. Only lib/WWW/MetaForge/ArcRaiders/Result/Quest.pm touched (11-line diff in from_hashref), no other lib/ files, no t/ files. Ticket left in-progress; not moved/handed off per instructions -- orchestrator to move after test-writer updates coverage.

